stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PENDING : create transaction<br/>(check fee exists & not paid)

    PENDING --> OTP_SENT : balance sufficient<br/>OTP generated & sent via email
    PENDING --> FAILED : insufficient balance<br/>OR fee already paid<br/>(HTTP 409 Conflict)
    PENDING --> CANCELLED : user cancels<br/>before OTP is sent

    OTP_SENT --> SUCCESS : correct OTP verified<br/>within 5 minutes
    OTP_SENT --> FAILED : wrong OTP<br/>(max attempts exceeded)
    OTP_SENT --> EXPIRED : OTP not verified<br/>within 5 minutes<br/>(HTTP 410 Gone)

    SUCCESS --> [*] : balance deducted<br/>fee status updated<br/>confirmation email sent
    FAILED --> [*]
    EXPIRED --> [*]
    CANCELLED --> [*]

    note right of SUCCESS
        Final state - triggers:
        - User Service: deduct balance
        - Fee Service: update paid_amount/status
        - RabbitMQ: publish confirmation email event
    end note

    note right of PENDING
        This is the "reservation" state
        used to lock TuitionFee.status = pending
        preventing a second concurrent payer
        (Scenario B in Transaction/Concurrency)
    end note
